<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ambhi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Taxiles, Omphis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ambhi was the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taxila">Taxila</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the late 4th century BCE, known to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> as Taxiles and also as Omphis. A rival of the neighbouring Paurava king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porus">Porus</a>, he submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> in 326 BCE and supplied troops and elephants for the campaign against Porus at the Hydaspes. Alexander confirmed him as ruler of his kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ambhi.jpg" alt="Ambhi" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Verdier 1651 Paris 1730 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taxiles_offering_presents_to_Alexander.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
